WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.881
Azure CLI scripts often run in CI/CD
systems, scheduled jobs,

2
00:00:05.961 --> 00:00:11.653
deployment agents, containers, and
operational workstations.

3
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:19.288
Each environment has different credential,
logging, network, and runtime behavior.

4
00:00:19.368 --> 00:00:25.784
Pipeline identities and service
connections should be scoped to the job,

5
00:00:25.864 --> 00:00:33.108
and production paths should be protected
with branch, tag, release, environment,

6
00:00:33.188 --> 00:00:34.947
and approval gates.

7
00:00:35.027 --> 00:00:41.029
Operational logs should identify the
automation identity, tenant,

8
00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:47.422
subscription, region, resource group,
target category, action, time,

9
00:00:47.502 --> 00:00:50.814
and result without exposing secrets.

10
00:00:50.894 --> 00:00:57.827
This evidence helps teams understand what
happened without spreading tokens,

11
00:00:57.907 --> 00:01:05.358
service principal credentials, private
configuration, or sensitive role details.

12
00:01:05.438 --> 00:01:12.268
In CI/CD, pay attention to command
echoing, debug modes, artifact retention,

13
00:01:12.348 --> 00:01:14.522
and who can read job logs.

14
00:01:14.602 --> 00:01:20.707
Azure Activity Logs, sign-in logs, audit
logs, service diagnostics,

15
00:01:20.787 --> 00:01:28.031
monitoring alerts, and access reviews help
teams understand what automation did.

16
00:01:28.111 --> 00:01:32.354
Monitoring should look for unusual
identities,

17
00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:35.849
unexpected subscriptions or regions,

18
00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:41.828
high-impact actions outside release
windows, repeated failures,

19
00:01:41.908 --> 00:01:48.738
unexpected RBAC changes, and service
behavior that differs from the expected

20
00:01:48.818 --> 00:01:50.681
deployment outcome.

21
00:01:50.761 --> 00:01:55.521
Incident response should cover credential
exposure,

22
00:01:55.601 --> 00:02:02.432
wrong-subscription changes, unexpected
role assignments, failed changes,

23
00:02:02.512 --> 00:02:05.823
and rollback or containment actions.

24
00:02:05.903 --> 00:02:10.664
Teams should know how to revoke or rotate
credentials,

25
00:02:10.744 --> 00:02:17.884
pause affected workflows, identify
impacted resources, review audit evidence,

26
00:02:17.964 --> 00:02:20.034
and update guardrails.

27
00:02:20.114 --> 00:02:26.841
Incidents and near misses should lead to
better validation, narrower roles,

28
00:02:26.921 --> 00:02:31.060
safer logging, and stronger review
processes.
